---
title: Compare the bell patterns
lang: en
---

## Listen for spacing

By the end of this lesson, you can describe the spacing of the practice bell pattern without treating it as a station instruction.

The practice bell makes two short tones with a gap between them. The file below is a synthetic tone, not a recording from a place or a person. In Lantern Marsh, keepers use this exercise to agree on words such as short and gap before they discuss a real station bell.

A [gap]{The quiet interval between two tones in a bell pattern.} belongs in your description as well as the tones.

--- Hear the practice bell

## Hear the practice bell

/assets/practice-bell.wav
title: Two practice tones
caption: Two synthetic tones separated by a quiet gap.
transcript: A short high tone sounds. A quiet gap follows. A second short high tone sounds. No speech is present.

Listen once, or use the transcript. Describe the pattern using the words tone and gap. Neither route through this exercise requires audio playback.

### Tones
as: accordion

The tones have the same pitch and length. Their sameness lets you focus on spacing.

### Gap

The quiet gap separates the tones. Do not count it as a third tone.

close: accordion

--- Count the tones

## Count the tones

A partner describes the file as "tone, gap, tone". Count the sounds they name, not the parts of the description.

### How many tones are in this practice pattern?
as: choice

(x) Two
feedback: The gap is quiet and adds no tone.
( ) Three
feedback: This counts the quiet gap as a sound.
( ) One continuous tone
feedback: The quiet gap separates the two sounds.

--- Describe a rhythm

## Describe a rhythm

Tap a pattern on your desk, or draw marks for it if tapping is uncomfortable. Ask a partner to describe the tones and gaps without copying your marks.

Compare their description with what you intended. Write down one ambiguity. You might need to explain whether a long space means a longer gap or a missed tap. This is a discussion exercise with no keyed answer.

Keep the discussion about spacing. The practice pattern does not authorise any route action.
